  - Removed [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m from the route and dropped the now-unused [38;5;153m./auth[39m import.
  - Added a two-line comment recording that the route is deliberately open, so the next reader doesn't file it as a bug
    and silently "fix" it back — that would break the dashboard script.
  - [38;5;153mauth.js[39m is left in place but is now unreferenced; [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m still exports fine if you want it back later.

  Verified with [38;5;153mnode --check server.js[39m (passes). There's no test or lint setup in this repo, so nothing else to run — I
  did not start the server or hit the route.

  One thing worth acting on separately: the protection is now entirely network topology, and "as far as I know" is doing
  the work. Worth confirming that the listener isn't reachable outside the office network — [38;5;153mapp.listen[39m binds all
  interfaces, so a load balancer, port-forward, or an SSRF-able service on the same network would reach it.

